    "title": "DSP8 disjoint distance-six multiplicity gate",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "After the proved distance-four and support-overlap deletions, every P>=25 target retains at least 11 disjoint distance-six edges in the antipodal-free class and at least two in the antipodal class. This forces respectively a same-target two-leaf star ideal and a same-target two-edge ideal; on P>=33 the two classes force pure disjoint-distance-six stars of degrees seven and five.",
